---
/**
 * P4 Development partners & NGOs: /partner-with-us/development-partners/ (T3, implements doc 04 matrix 4.1).
 * C1 to C14 in order, as the numbered table in doc 06 P4, without C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine), which the audience pages leave to Home since WP47.
 * WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): every CMF band stays, each states its point once. Gone: the In Short summary, the fit check, the evidence-and-fit
 * brief, the 2015 pilot quote with its caveat, the second survey of the standard inclusions and the restated three-step mechanism. Five FAQs, not nine.
 * WP35 (cycle-12 review): the trial and the survey are shown once, as tiles in Results at a Glance; the proof band that restated them is a one-line strip of links (#proof-band). The WSDFM tile is gone
 * from the glance (its 71% is program records, read beside the trial's 63.1%; the Kosovo program result takes its place).
 * WP36 (cycle-13 reviews): each figure is stated once. The Kosovo result (102 of 150) is on its Proof in Practice card, so the glance's program-record tile is UNDP YES, Korail (PR-03: a program with UNDP, one of the development partners in PA-01)
 * and the Kosovo tile is gone; the mechanism card says "Placement support into ..."; the three pains are statements ("What Gets in the Way"); the cost question has the one-line route answer and a link to the hub FAQ.
 * WP37 (cycle-14 review): the women-and-marginalized-groups answer no longer restates the three program figures (Proof in Practice, directly above, shows them); it says so and keeps the scope of the trial.
 * WP39 (cycle-16 review): "What Your Portfolio Gets" is three short cards (IncludesBand), not the funder concern / what is included / practical benefit matrix.
 * WP40 (cycle-17 review): "Reporting and Review" says what the reports and reviews do instead of pointing at the overview; the closing "It doesn’t have to be this way." line of the cost band is gone.
 * WP42 (cycle-19 reviews): "Our Approach" is the two shared sentences with the tracking said as the cards say it ("Partners receive monthly reports and outcome tracking after each course, as agreed in the program scope."; POSITIONING.developmentPartners,
 * declared whole in scripts/check-facts.mjs), and the YouthWIDE explanation still follows it; the ">4×" tile (the glance's fourth) quotes the multiplier and the nine-trial average only (the +10.3 is the lead tile's: RC-06a's glance note).
 * WP43 (cycle-20 review): the cost-of-waiting heading is "Build Work Entry into the Training Budget" (the old one, "Training Without Placement Spends Budget Without Earnings", was an absolute claim; the two cards under it still carry the claims).
 * WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): the page opens with its own proof and goes straight to its offer. The Cost of Waiting band ("Build Work Entry into the Training Budget") and the Imagine band ("What Your Monthly Report
 * Could Show") are gone; Home carries them. Nothing on this page depended on them: the monthly reports, follow-up surveys and documentary evidence (where available) are stated in the "Questions Partners Ask"
 * answers, "Results Your Evaluators Can Check" and "Reporting and Review".
 * WP48 (cycle-23 review, item 25): the ">4×" tile's label says what is compared ("The employment effect for women offered a place, against the 2.3-point average across nine vocational-training trials"), so RC-06a's glance note
 * ("Against 2.3 percentage points on average ...") repeated it and is gone.
 * WP49 (cycle-24 review): the problem band is headed "Show Who Reaches Paid Work" and its first two cards "Training Must Connect to Paid Work" and "Barriers Can Interrupt Training" (the earlier headings stated sector-wide conclusions; the card bodies are unchanged);
 * "What Your Portfolio Gets" says in its first card that one delivery partner connects training, mentoring and placement support (the hours stay in the delivery model above); the ">4×" tile is the fourth tile of "Results at a Glance" (a
 * single tile needs no "More Results" heading); the closing steps band is "What Happens Next".
 * WP50 (cycle-25 review): the problem band's lead says "... keeping hard-to-reach groups engaged, is the hard part." (it said "... groups in, ...").
 * WP51 (cycle-26 review, Kimi P2): the Track Record band opens with the shared origin line, "Since 2014, from a Copenhagen launch to programs in 15 countries and territories." (ORIGIN_SHORT, as on Governments and Foundations), in place of
 * "Launched in Copenhagen in 2014."; PartnerGuideBand no longer swaps in the launch alone for a band that shows SC-03's tile (Investors prints the same shared line in its own band, InvestorGuide: Grok m1).
 * WP52 (cycle-27 review, Kimi M2): the ">4×" tile is gone from the glance, which is now three tiles in one row (the trial, the survey and UNDP YES, Korail); its comparison is the +10.3 tile's note ("More than four times the 2.3-point average across
 * nine vocational-training trials."). Foundations and Governments never showed the ">4×" tile, and Home's first slide keeps its own (there it is the slide's benchmark, not a repeat of a glance tile).
 * WP52 (cycle-27 reviews, Gemini): the "Where They Work" card says "Placement support into local, remote and global work, ..." (it said "... local, remote, overseas and freelance work", not the site's usual wording); the "Choose Where to Start" band's eyebrow is "Options"
 * (see the Governments page).
 * WP53 (owner follow-up, 2026-10-16): the "Where They Work" card says "local, remote and global work" once, in its title; the text is "Placement support and outcome tracking for 12 months after each course." (as Home's card, with the months from PD-02).
 */
import PartnerGlance from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGlance.astro';
import PairedEvidence from '../../../components/pages/partners/PairedEvidence.astro';
import DueDiligenceView from '../../../components/pages/hub/DueDiligenceView.astro';
import LearnerVoice from '../../../components/pages/impact/LearnerVoice.astro';
import LandingLayout from '../../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../../components/sections/HeroBand.astro';
import DefinitionBand from '../../../components/sections/DefinitionBand.astro';
import ProblemBand from '../../../components/sections/ProblemBand.astro';
import MechanismBand from '../../../components/sections/MechanismBand.astro';
import CaseStudyCarousel from '../../../components/sections/CaseStudyCarousel.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import FAQBand from '../../../components/sections/FAQBand.astro';
import NextStepsBand from '../../../components/sections/NextStepsBand.astro';
import CTABand from '../../../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import SessionAgenda from '../../../components/ui/SessionAgenda.astro';
import GainsPains from '../../../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import PartnerGuideBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGuideBand.astro';
import SubBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/SubBand.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/pages/partners/Callout.astro';
import CopyText from '../../../components/pages/partners/CopyText.astro';
import OfferCards from '../../../components/pages/partners/OfferCards.astro';
import RouteLink from '../../../components/pages/partners/RouteLink.astro';
import Reinforcement from '../../../components/pages/partners/Reinforcement.astro';
import PageEnhancements from '../../../components/pages/partners/PageEnhancements.astro';
import { HOURS, LINKS, TRACKING_MONTHS, funderOptionCards, meta } from '../../../components/pages/partners/partners';
import { ACCOUNTABILITY, HEADLINE, MICRO_COMMITMENT, POSITIONING, PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE, VALUE_PROPOSITION, WB_KOSOVO } from '../../../data/copy';
import { fact } from '../../../data/facts';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../../../lib/faq';
import { cta } from '../../../lib/mailto';
import { webPage } from '../../../lib/schema';

const PATH = '/partner-with-us/development-partners/';
const primary = cta('discovery');

const { title, description } = meta(
  'Youth Employment for Development Partners',
  'A randomized trial of a predecessor program found women offered a place were 10.3 percentage points more likely to be employed. Results you can report.',
);

// WP52 (cycle-27 review, Kimi M2): the ">4×" tile (RC-06a) showed the trial result a second time beside the "+10.3 percentage points" tile (the third reviewer in three cycles to say so), so it is gone and its comparison is the +10.3 tile's note.
// The note is read from RC-06a's glance label ("The employment effect for women offered a place was more than four times the 2.3-point average across nine vocational-training trials"), never retyped, and the build stops if the label stops ending that way.
const benchmark = /(more than four times the 2\.3-point average across nine vocational-training trials)$/.exec(fact('RC-06a').stat?.glance?.label ?? '')?.[1];
if (!benchmark) throw new Error('Development Partners: the RC-06a glance label no longer ends "... more than four times the 2.3-point average across nine vocational-training trials"; update the +10.3 tile\'s note');
const benchmarkNote = `${benchmark[0].toUpperCase()}${benchmark.slice(1)}.`;

// Q8-route: the one-line cost answer with a link to the partner hub FAQ, which keeps the full answer (WP36).
// Q6-development-partners: the women-and-marginalized-groups answer points to Proof in Practice above instead of stating its three program figures again (WP37); the bank's shared Q6 keeps the figures.
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q1-development-partners', 'Q6-development-partners', 'Q3', 'Q10', 'Q8-route'];
---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={PATH}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Partner with Us', href: LINKS.hub }, { label: 'Development Partners and NGOs' }]}
  jsonLd={[webPage({ path: PATH, name: title, description }), faqJsonLd('development-partners', PATH, FAQ_IDS)]}
  stickyCta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
>
  <!-- C1 · Identity hook -->
  <HeroBand
    audience="For Development Partners and NGOs"
    title={HEADLINE.developmentPartners}
    lead={VALUE_PROPOSITION.developmentPartners}
    cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
    artSeed="partners-development"
  />
  <RouteLink kicker="See the Program" label="How YouthWIDE Works" href={LINKS.youthwide} />
  <!-- GEO · What is CodersTrust? -->
  <DefinitionBand />
  <PartnerGlance
    lead={[{ id: 'RC-02', href: '/impact/independent-evaluation/', note: benchmarkNote, also: ['RC-06a'] }, { id: 'OC-01', href: '/impact/outcomes-2026/' }, { id: 'PR-03', href: LINKS.caseUndp }]}
    more={[]}
  />
  <LearnerVoice story="adrian-afraham" excerpt="Following my completion of the course, I successfully secured my very first freelance job, which was followed by an enticing job offer." program="Graphic Designing course, CodersTrust Bangladesh" tone="white" />

  <!-- C2 · Problem -->
  <ProblemBand
    title="Show Who Reaches Paid Work"
    bluf="You can count who enrolled. Showing who is earning, and keeping hard-to-reach groups engaged, is the hard part."
    factIds={['PX-01']}
  >
    <GainsPains
      slot="lead"
      pains={[
        // WP48 (cycle-23 review): "Enrollment targets are often met, while employment results lag behind." was a claim about the whole sector; the card says only what the page can stand behind.
        // WP49 (cycle-24 review): the two card titles were broad sector conclusions too ("Skills Programs Miss Their Employment Targets", "The Hardest-to-Reach Groups Drop Out"), as was the band heading; they say what the partner needs, and the bodies stay.
        { q: 'Training must connect to paid work', text: 'Enrollment is easy to count. Paid work is not.' },
        { q: 'Barriers can interrupt training', text: 'Computer skills, devices, connectivity and social barriers can keep learners from joining or staying.' },
        { q: 'Outcomes are hard to audit', text: 'Without a baseline and documentary evidence, evaluators have little to check.' },
      ]}
    />
  </ProblemBand>

  <!-- C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine) are left to Home since WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15). -->

  <!-- C5 · Guide. WP44 (cycle-21 review): no empathy line; the band opens with the origin line. WP51 (cycle-26 review): that line is the one Governments and Foundations print, "Since 2014, from a Copenhagen launch to programs in 15 countries and territories." (ORIGIN_SHORT), in place of the launch alone. -->
  <PartnerGuideBand
    stats={['SC-01', 'SC-03']}
    method={{ text: 'Our TalentLEAP method organizes skills into career paths.', link: { label: 'How TalentLEAP Works', href: LINKS.talentleap } }}
    partnerGroup="development"
    strip
  />

  <!-- C6 · Mechanism (YouthWIDE) -->
  <MechanismBand
    title="An Integrated Path from Training to Earnings"
    positioning={POSITIONING.developmentPartners}
    lead="YouthWIDE is the program through which funders deploy the CodersTrust model in a country; it builds on results from earlier programs in Bangladesh and Kosovo."
    blocks={[
      { label: 'Who We Reach', title: 'Priority Groups', text: 'Priority groups are agreed with you in co-design; women are a priority in every group.', icon: 'users' },
      { label: 'How We Reach Them', title: 'Existing Labs and Colleges', text: 'Outreach and selection with local partners, then blended delivery in existing labs and colleges.', icon: 'graduation-cap' },
      { label: 'What We Deliver', title: 'Certification and Mentoring', text: `${HOURS} training hours per certification, then three months of milestone-based mentoring and placement support.`, icon: 'award' },
      { label: 'Where They Work', title: 'Local, Remote and Global Work', text: `Placement support and outcome tracking for ${TRACKING_MONTHS} months after each course.`, icon: 'globe' },
    ]}
    link={{ label: 'How Our Model Works', href: LINKS.model }}
  />

  <!-- C7 · Proof: the trial and survey results are the tiles above; this strip links the full evidence (WP35, cycle-12 review) -->
  <PairedEvidence
    id="proof-band"
    eyebrow="The Evidence"
    title="See the Evidence Behind the Results"
    items={[]}
    broader={[
      { label: 'Read the Trial Results', href: LINKS.trial },
      { label: 'Impact Survey 2026', href: LINKS.outcomes },
    ]}
    broaderLabel="The evidence behind the results"
  />
  <CaseStudyCarousel
    title="Proof in Practice"
    items={[
      { title: 'Women’s Skill Development for Freelancing Marketplace (WSDFM)', program: 'Commissioned by Porticus', factId: 'PR-01', href: LINKS.caseWsdfm },
      { title: 'Women in Online Work, Kosovo', program: 'World Bank Group', factId: 'PR-02', note: WB_KOSOVO, href: LINKS.caseWow },
      { title: 'Her Power', program: 'ICT Division / Department of ICT (DoICT)', factId: 'PR-05', href: LINKS.caseHerPower },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C8 · Features to benefits. WP39 (cycle-16 review): three short cards in place of the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix, in the order of the three pains in C2 (training must connect to paid work; barriers can interrupt training;
       outcomes are hard to audit). Each sentence rests on the register: PD-01 (mentoring and placement support alongside the training; WP49, cycle-24 review: the first card says only that one delivery partner connects them, because the 100 hours
       per certification are in the delivery model above), PD-02 and PD-10 (outreach and selection, tracks from employer demand), PD-12 (safeguarding specified per program), PD-08 and PD-09 (monthly reports, baseline, follow-up surveys,
       documentary evidence where available). -->
  <IncludesBand
    title="What Your Portfolio Gets"
    cards={[
      { icon: 'route', title: 'Training, Mentoring and Placement Support', text: 'One delivery partner connects training, mentoring and placement support.', facts: ['PD-01'] },
      { icon: 'map-pin', title: 'Accessible Local Delivery', text: 'Outreach, accessible selection and tracks chosen from employer demand, with safeguarding agreed for each program.', facts: ['PD-02', 'PD-10', 'PD-12'] },
      { icon: 'clipboard-check', title: 'Results Your Evaluators Can Check', text: 'Baseline data, follow-up surveys and monthly reports, with documentary evidence where available, as agreed in the program scope.', facts: ['PD-08', 'PD-09'] },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C9 · Objections -->
  <FAQBand
    audience="development-partners"
    ids={FAQ_IDS}
    title="Questions Partners Ask"
    allLink={{ label: 'Safeguarding, Governance and Due Diligence', href: LINKS.governance }}
  />

  <!-- C10 · Differentiation: the positioning statement opens C6; the comparison table is on Home and Investors only (WP30c). -->

  <!-- C11 · Offer -->
  <OfferCards eyebrow="Options" title="Choose Where to Start" lead={PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE} cards={funderOptionCards()} recommended={0} />
  <SubBand tone="airy" pull>
    <Callout eyebrow="Accountability"><CopyText block={ACCOUNTABILITY} /></Callout>
  </SubBand>

  <!-- C12 · Risk reversal (immediately before C13): WP34 (cycle-11 review): the four diligence cards repeated what this page's bands state, so one item and a link stand in. WP45 (cycle-21 review): the hub's reporting band (#review-cycle) is gone,
       so the callout below states the reporting and review once and has no link to it (the due-diligence item above links to Governance and Accountability). -->
  <DueDiligenceView brief id="due-diligence" />
  <SubBand>
    <Callout eyebrow="Reporting and Review">
      <p data-fact="PD-08 PD-11">For supported cohorts, monthly reports track progress; quarterly reviews guide corrective action and any expansion.</p>
    </Callout>
  </SubBand>

  <!-- C13 · Call to action -->
  <CTABand
    id="cta"
    heading="Let’s Design Your First Cohort"
    cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Read the evidence', href: LINKS.evidence }}
    micro={MICRO_COMMITMENT}
  >
    <SessionAgenda />
  </CTABand>

  <!-- C14 · Next steps -->
  <!-- WP46 (cycle-22 review): the grant-funded timing (about three weeks to agreement, 6–8 weeks from signing to training, procurement on the agency's own timeline) is stated once on this page, in the steps and lead below; the C13 urgency line that repeated it is gone (as on Foundations, whose steps band is the same). -->
  <NextStepsBand timing={false} />
  <Reinforcement logos={false} reminder={false} />

  <PageEnhancements />
</LandingLayout>
